92186415645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415673 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "47d1b44e-be04-5aae-bd0c-c0fa80e8a07b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415674 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415674 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415674 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415674 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "77c94cbf-f9ef-59ad-9086-7c8d91862986" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415675 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415675 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415675 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415675 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415675 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415675 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415675 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415675 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415675 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9bc8f0e0-f5cb-5cee-aa30-efe616caf6e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415676 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415676 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124313" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415676 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415676 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fb/fbc6ddf87d5f5502db656242222dca27fb33ded5d3bdcf372b70ef10eda07624.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a three-quarter circle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(-1,-3)$ to the point $(-4,0),$ shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415676 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "19c93f12-207e-5d48-9d03-3dc16bfb7738" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415676 #edb/ref 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-4$ and ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-4)-(-1)=-3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415677 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415677 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124187" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415677 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415677 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=17,$ ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=7,$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=5,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415677 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28b25a72-e404-5d69-993b-a9b2c8d9ba39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415677 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 17 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+5-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 17 & =-7+5-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 19 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-19.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415678 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415678 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124183" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415678 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415678 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=14$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-6,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415678 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41a5f2bb-63fd-5596-b20f-47e35c05d2ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415678 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =14-(-6) \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415679 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415679 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124290" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415679 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415679 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/4d/4d1c20f44c7a092275f200737